# 💻 Building and Running

## Prerequisites

A Linux environment or WSL installation with the required xv6 RISC-V development tools.

Typical requirements include:

* RISC-V GCC toolchain
* QEMU
* GNU Make
* Git

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone <YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL>
```

Navigate to the project:

```bash
cd xv6-riscv
```

Build the kernel:

```bash
make
```

Run xv6:

```bash
make qemu
```

---

# 🧪 Running Tests

Run the standard xv6 regression tests:

```bash
make qemu
```

Then execute:

```bash
usertests
```

The project also contains dedicated tests for the enhanced functionality.

Refer to the corresponding source/test files in the repository for the exact commands and test cases implemented for each feature.

