# 🎓 Learning Outcomes

Through this project, the following concepts were explored through practical kernel-level implementation:

1. Understanding the internal structure of an operating-system kernel.
2. Modifying kernel process-management mechanisms.
3. Implementing and evaluating CPU scheduling policies.
4. Understanding user-kernel interaction through system calls.
5. Designing system-call tracing mechanisms.
6. Collecting and analyzing kernel performance metrics.
7. Developing OS-level benchmarks.
8. Performing regression testing after kernel modifications.
9. Debugging and validating low-level C code.
10. Working with RISC-V-based educational operating systems.

